    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "menu\nOCTOBER 17, 1950\nPan American Management Club\nSAN FRANCISCO\nwelcomes\nVice President Harold M. Bixby\nVice President Erwin E. Balluder\nVice President Henry J. Friendly\nVice President Willis G. Lipscomb\nCover Design\nby Lillian Sader.\nOne of America's leading\nyoung artists, Miss Sader\ncombines a deft color touch\nwith a sensitive flair\nfor intricate design.\nFor the Orient\nshe has created\na unique tableau of\nthese familiar attractions—\nTypical Chinese Gateway\nDaibutsu-giant image of Buddha\nFujiyama\nThe Torii-formal Japanese Gateway\nGeisha Girl in Japanese Garden\nA Chinese Pagoda, Pedicab\nPhilippine Rice Field\nSampan and Siamese Temples\nVin Grenache Rose\nCelery\nAssorted Olives\nItalian Salami\nCarrots en Branch\nImported Swiss Cheese\nPickles\nSupreme of Melon Flavored with Fresh Mint\nChef's Special Salad\nBroiled Choice New York Cut Steak\nFresh Mushroom Sauce\nBaked Idaho Potato in Jacket\nFrench Cut String Beans au Beurre\nFrench Roll\nButter Gem\nCoffee\nDessert\nTea\nMilk\nComplete set of menus\nsuitable for framing may be\nobtained upon request\nPAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS O\nPRINTED IN U.S. A."
    ],
